  "practice": [
    "Say ঈ three times with its modern ee/i sound: i, i, i.",
    "Practice the vowel sign: ন + ী = নী, দ + ী = দী, ব + ী = বী, and শ + ী = শী.",
    "Read the pairs ই/ঈ and ি/ী aloud; in modern speech their vowel sounds are generally the same.",
    "Compare দিন (day) and দীন (poor/destitute), then memorize which spelling each word uses."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ঈ is called দীর্ঘ ঈ (dirgho i) and has an ee/i sound.",
    "In modern spoken Bangla, ঈ and ই are generally pronounced the same; the difference is mainly in spelling.",
    "After a consonant, ঈ becomes ী, called দীর্ঘ ঈ-কার: ন + ী = নী.",
    "The spellings ি (ই-কার) and ী (ঈ-কার) normally have essentially the same modern pronunciation, so the correct spelling must be learned with each word."
  ]
